NIST/SEMATECH e-Handbook of Statistical Methods, chapter 2, Measurement Process Characterization, with supporting chapters on process modelling and exploratory data analysis. [Chapter 2 and detailed contents](https://www.itl.nist.gov/div898/handbook/mpc/mpc.htm) · [Handbook contents](https://www.itl.nist.gov/div898/handbook/).

Read chapter 2 completely through its linked sections: characterization, measurement control, calibration, gauge repeatability and reproducibility studies, uncertainty analysis, and case studies. Work the supplied numerical examples and consult their references. Use the process-modelling material for regression assumptions and residual diagnostics when the calibration reading calls for it.

This is a substantial open technical handbook, not a single summary webpage. Record the section title and stable page address for a result being reconstructed. The old frames-based index can be unhelpful; the direct chapter page exposes the reading structure.

NIST-produced federal material is generally public domain in the United States; preserve attribution and separately identified contributions, data, and software terms. Official contents checked on 28 October 2026. The reading remains external.

